# dom0: /etc/qubes/policy.d/30-wormhole.policy
# Sorts before 90-default.policy, which denies everything.
#
# THIS FILE is what confers the capability. The clients ship to every qube
# inheriting the template, but they are inert without a line here: an ungranted
# caller gets rc 126 "Request refused" and no disposable is ever created.
# Install broadly, grant narrowly.
#
# The TARGET must name the DVM template. A bare `@dispvm` rule REFUSES a caller
# that names one -- verified against live dom0, not just the policy parser.
#
# The two directions are SEPARATE SERVICES on purpose, so a qube can be granted
# one and not the other:
#   wormhole.Send is an exfiltration primitive -- it moves data OUT.
#   wormhole.Recv is an injection primitive    -- it brings untrusted data IN.
# A hardened qube may reasonably be allowed to pull files in while remaining
# unable to send any out. Grant each direction deliberately.

wormhole.Send  +file  personal  @dispvm:wormhole_dvm  allow
wormhole.Recv  +file  personal  @dispvm:wormhole_dvm  allow

# Add one line per additional qube, per direction, e.g.:
# wormhole.Recv  +file  vault  @dispvm:wormhole_dvm  allow

# Catch-alls. Must be last. Deny every unlisted verb and every unlisted caller.
wormhole.Send  *      @anyvm    @anyvm                deny
wormhole.Recv  *      @anyvm    @anyvm                deny
